# 1EG Passport — durable-URL redirect host (Cloudflare Pages `_redirects`)
# Project Blackbook HK09 Phase 2A. Governing repo: GreenglassVarano/greenglass-varano-preconstruction-kb
#
# THE DURABLE PUBLIC CONTRACT IS THE HOSTNAME AND PATH, PERMANENTLY:
#     https://passport.greenglassvarano.com/1EG/<RecordID>
# The SharePoint destination below is REPLACEABLE IMPLEMENTATION DETAIL.
#
# STATUS CODES — deliberate:
#   302 for the durable-host -> current-SharePoint hop. NEVER 301.
#       A cacheable permanent redirect would burn today's SharePoint URL into
#       clients and weaken future portability. The hostname is permanent; the
#       backend is not.
#   301 only to canonicalise an ALTERNATE HOSTING hostname onto the durable one.
#
# ORDER MATTERS — first match wins. Specific rules precede general ones.
#
# THE REDIRECT HOST IS DELIBERATELY DUMB. It does not validate that a Record ID
# exists. Well-formed-but-absent and malformed IDs are both forwarded; the SPFx
# Passport page decides what to show.

# --- /1EG/<RecordID> : the governed contract ------------------------------------
# Trailing-slash form first, so /1EG/1EG-0001/ keeps the Record ID.
/1EG/:id/  https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx?p=:id  302
/1EG/:id   https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx?p=:id  302

# --- everything else under /1EG : Passport Landing, no Record ID ----------------
# Covers /1EG/ (empty id) and nested paths such as /1EG/a/b — never fabricate an ID.
/1EG/*     https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302
/1EG       https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302

# --- bare host and every other namespace : Passport Landing ---------------------
# Covers / and wrong namespaces such as /wrong/1EG-0001.
/*         https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302

# --- CUTOVER-ONLY canonicalisation — DO NOT ENABLE DURING STAGING ---------------
# Enabling this while passport.greenglassvarano.com still points at GitHub Pages
# would make the Pages staging deployment untestable: every *.pages.dev request
# would 301 away to the old host. Uncomment ONLY at cutover, replacing <project>.
#
# https://<project>.pages.dev/*  https://passport.greenglassvarano.com/:splat  301
